The Memphis area is forecasted that we will be experiencing below freezing temperatures/ levels. We wanted to make you aware of the possibility of pipes freezing and potentially bursting within your vacant property. Should this happen, it could lead to flooding, ceiling, flooring, or structural damage (sheet rock, joists, sub-flooring, etc.)&nbsp;<br />
<br />
To lessen the possibility of this happening, we strongly recommend winterizing your vacant property. We have vendors who are able to perform this service for a flat rate of $140.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
The service includes:&nbsp;<br />
<br />
* Draining the water heater&nbsp;<br />
* Replacing the water still remaining in the the faucet traps and toilet traps with an anti-freeze solution to keep the traps from bursting while still functioning as a barrier against sewer gases&nbsp;<br />
* Disconnecting the main supply line at the water meter to drain and clear water from the lines&nbsp;<br />
* Shutting off water supply to the house at the street&nbsp;<br />
* Placing notices/stickers at every fixture to make others aware to not attempt to use the water while vacant.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Again, this service is strongly recommended to better prevent costly damages and longer vacancy periods. We do require your approval to perform this service.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Though taking these precautions may not guarantee that your vacant property will not suffer any damages due to extreme winter conditions, it is an extra precaution that you will be less likely to have such damages occur.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Please reply TO ALL with either your approval or dismissal of this service offered.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Please contact me with any questions or concerns you may have.